From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: owner <owner@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:23:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Smartfill fork: multi-field logins and saved entry
 steps (grokbot:recipe)

Personal, unofficial modification of the browser extension (base: browser-v2026.10.2).

- A login's plain-named custom fields are typed into the best-matching control
  (case- and accent-insensitive, exact before partial, ties left empty, never a
  password box). Bitwarden's rule syntax and linked fields behave as before.
- A login with a grokbot:recipe custom field runs its saved entry steps instead
  of the heuristic fill: fill, click, wait, keypad, press; values username,
  password, totp, field:<name>, text:<words>. Same format as the Grok Bot
  connector.
- Steps continue after a page load only if the page still matches the login's
  saved addresses, the vault is unlocked and the tab is in front. Recipes never
  run on page-load fills, nor for shared (organization) logins.
- The build names itself 'Bitwarden Smartfill (unofficial fork)' and uses its
  own Firefox add-on id.

See apps/browser/SMARTFILL.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
